From 550bf64092d1374e121aa48a2758ff6847ca16f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:27:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09112/11362] Close the hole the --no-verify fix opened:
 restore determinations on the checkpoint path

Found by the guard refusing my own commit. A test run had rewritten 13 historical
artifacts and stripped the fabrication-gate quarantine from five -- exp833,
exp1736, exp3361, exp3377, exp3392 each lost `flagged_adversarial: true` plus
`corrigendum_note` and `corrigendum_pending`. exp2824 silently changed a metric
(`tier_low` to `tier_transfer`, 0.5 to 0.8). Everything else in the diffs was
fresh timestamps, so the only real content of the rewrite was the deletion of
recorded review judgements. All 13 restored from HEAD.

THE HOLE IS MINE AND IT IS NOW CLOSED. Earlier today the conductor's checkpoint
commit was changed to `--no-verify`, because pre-commit's stash-restore cycle had
destroyed an outer-loop session's work twice in one hour. That is right for a
commit whose only job is preserving work. It also skips
determination-preservation-lint -- so the next checkpoint would have published
this exact damage silently, with no refusal and nobody reading a diff. I removed
the guard that would have caught the thing that happened hours later.

`git_commit_and_push` already called `_restore_dropped_determinations()` before
its own `--no-verify` for precisely this reason. The checkpoint path did not. It
does now, before staging.

Restore rather than refuse, deliberately. A checkpoint that refuses leaves the
work uncommitted and vulnerable, which is the failure the checkpoint block exists
to prevent. Restoring keeps both: the new numbers land and the determination
survives.

The general lesson, and this is the fourth recurrence of test-run record damage:
skipping a hook suite to protect one property can silently drop another. When you
disable verification on a path, enumerate what that path was getting from the
hooks and re-add each protection you still need directly. `--no-verify` is not a
scalpel unless you make it one.
